<%#
  Cookbook:: consul
  Template:: resolv.conf.erb
  Local dnsmasq is the SOLE resolver. dnsmasq itself fails over to direct
  Pi-holes if CoreDNS is unreachable, so we don't need to list them here.
  Listing them here would let libc / Go's net.Resolver / etc. bypass the
  CoreDNS round-robin and hit Pi-holes directly, causing imbalanced LAN
  load (one Pi-hole at ~64%, the other at ~36% seen previously).
%>
# Managed by cinc/chef -- consul::dns
search <%= @search %>
nameserver <%= @listen_address %>
